From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 23:44:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Drain Leaf config reloads at tick boundaries

Apply queued Leaf reloads before a tick begins, after all world jobs from the previous tick have joined. Avoid the general task executor because it can also execute work mid-tick.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
index 45d9f1292616cd29c7e81edeec5368d044fd8086..f5f7def06675eb3698fd8450f87cb0470dc1888f 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/server/MinecraftServer.java
@@ -1713,6 +1713,7 @@ public abstract class MinecraftServer extends ReentrantBlockableEventLoop<TickTa
 
     protected void tickServer(final BooleanSupplier haveTime) {
         org.spigotmc.WatchdogThread.tick(); // Spigot
+        org.dreeam.leaf.config.LeafConfig.runPendingReloads(); // Pyzh - Reload only after the previous tick's world jobs have joined.
         long nano = Util.getNanos();
         int emptyTickThreshold = this.pauseWhenEmptySeconds() * 20;
         this.removeDisabledPluginsBlockingSleep(); // Paper - API to allow/disallow tick sleeping
